WEBVTT

1
00:00:17,760 --> 00:00:19,840
In Mukdahan province,

2
00:00:19,920 --> 00:00:22,240
let us all support the search of Chompoo,

3
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:27,080
the three-year-old girl who's disappeared
without a trace from home.

4
00:00:31,240 --> 00:00:34,480
At first, we thought it was
just a simple missing-child case.

5
00:00:36,720 --> 00:00:40,800
But it turned into a major event
that captured the nation's attention.

6
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:44,000
Viewers, regarding Chompoo…

7
00:00:45,600 --> 00:00:49,360
the authorities immediately deployed
forces up there, searching day and night…

8
00:00:49,440 --> 00:00:50,400
Check the channel.

9
00:00:50,480 --> 00:00:51,960
…through the forests for her.

10
00:00:52,560 --> 00:00:53,600
They found nothing.

11
00:00:55,280 --> 00:00:59,960
{\an8}We have interviewed
a total of 384 witnesses.

12
00:01:00,600 --> 00:01:03,800
If it's a kidnapping,
the culprit is absolutely heartless.

13
00:01:04,560 --> 00:01:06,480
Uncle Phol was just her uncle-in-law.

14
00:01:06,560 --> 00:01:07,800
Haven't seen you in days.

15
00:01:07,880 --> 00:01:11,280
Out of the blue, the girl's
case turned into a beauty pageant contest.

16
00:01:13,240 --> 00:01:16,560
Uncle Phol, look at the camera.
Make a handsome pose.

17
00:01:16,640 --> 00:01:17,840
Check, check, check.

18
00:01:17,920 --> 00:01:20,320
-Hello, Uncle Phol.
-We love Uncle Phol.

19
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:23,000
I said, "Gosh! You should be
a star with a face like this."

20
00:01:23,080 --> 00:01:25,240
"Tao Ngoi" by Jintara and Uncle Phol!

21
00:01:25,320 --> 00:01:27,480
Uncle Phol!

22
00:01:29,600 --> 00:01:30,680
Dance!

23
00:01:30,760 --> 00:01:32,960
YouTubers came around.

24
00:01:33,040 --> 00:01:35,600
You just came back. Let me hug you.

25
00:01:37,640 --> 00:01:40,000
Everyone focused on Uncle Phol.

26
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:45,240
They must've completely forgotten
what had happened to the child.

27
00:01:52,920 --> 00:01:54,080
Speed<i>.</i>

28
00:01:54,160 --> 00:01:57,280
CHAIPHON WHIPHA
"UNCLE PHOL," CHOMPOO'S UNCLE

29
00:01:57,360 --> 00:01:59,680
Sound ready? Rolling.

30
00:01:59,760 --> 00:02:00,960
Hello.

31
00:02:04,640 --> 00:02:07,000
CHOMPOO: LOST & FORGOTTEN

32
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:15,480
When I first moved to Kok Kork…

33
00:02:15,560 --> 00:02:16,400
KOK KORK VILLAGE

34
00:02:16,480 --> 00:02:18,760
…it was as if I'd moved to a hidden city.

35
00:02:18,840 --> 00:02:21,400
There was no connection
to the outside world.

36
00:02:21,480 --> 00:02:26,280
KOK KORK VILLAGE
NORTHEASTERN REGION, THAILAND

37
00:02:27,560 --> 00:02:31,400
ANAMAI WONGSRICHA
CHOMPOO'S FATHER

38
00:02:31,480 --> 00:02:34,120
Here, we rely on each other.
We help each other.

39
00:02:34,920 --> 00:02:36,720
I help you, and you help me.

40
00:02:39,560 --> 00:02:40,880
NALIN NGOENNAM
"AUNT THORN"

41
00:02:40,960 --> 00:02:44,880
We all know each other.
Our village is related by blood,

42
00:02:44,960 --> 00:02:48,240
and most of the men are sons-in-law.

43
00:02:52,240 --> 00:02:54,280
We're poor, but we're happy.

44
00:02:54,360 --> 00:02:57,520
When someone cooks a pot of food,
we share it with each other.

45
00:02:57,600 --> 00:03:01,400
My children, grandchildren,
and Chompoo had meals together.

46
00:03:03,920 --> 00:03:06,400
Chompoo, she's so innocent.

47
00:03:06,480 --> 00:03:08,600
How could someone do this to her?

48
00:03:11,040 --> 00:03:14,360
The truth of what happened in Kok Kork,

49
00:03:14,920 --> 00:03:18,640
I and those who were at the scene
and were a part of it

50
00:03:19,840 --> 00:03:22,960
would know best
about what happened in Kok Kork.

51
00:03:31,520 --> 00:03:34,800
And as for my last memory that day,

52
00:03:35,720 --> 00:03:37,840
my last memory of Chompoo…

53
00:03:39,320 --> 00:03:43,880
{\an8}MAY 11, 2020
6:00 A.M., THE DAY OF THE DISAPPEARANCE

54
00:03:43,960 --> 00:03:47,920
…I was on my tractor,
about to go out to level the rice field.

55
00:03:50,600 --> 00:03:53,560
Chompoo came out and called to me.

56
00:03:55,440 --> 00:03:56,520
She said…

57
00:03:59,680 --> 00:04:01,560
"Come back home soon."

58
00:04:01,640 --> 00:04:03,920
"Don't forget to buy me some snacks."

59
00:04:05,440 --> 00:04:07,920
That's the last memory I have of her.

60
00:04:10,480 --> 00:04:11,960
I've never forgotten it.

61
00:04:15,920 --> 00:04:20,240
Then I drove off to do my work,
leveling the rice field.

62
00:04:31,800 --> 00:04:36,160
And then, around nine or ten
in the morning, my phone rang.

63
00:04:36,240 --> 00:04:37,840
I answered it.

64
00:04:37,920 --> 00:04:40,040
They told me to hurry home quick,

65
00:04:40,120 --> 00:04:42,400
because they couldn't find Chompoo.

66
00:04:44,840 --> 00:04:47,440
I really wasn't too worried at first.

67
00:04:48,480 --> 00:04:51,400
She might be just playing in the village,

68
00:04:51,960 --> 00:04:54,000
or playing with some older children.

69
00:04:59,720 --> 00:05:02,760
She loved watching cartoons
and playing with toys.

70
00:05:03,920 --> 00:05:06,080
She would pretend to sell things.

71
00:05:10,920 --> 00:05:13,440
She was very close
with her older sister, Sading.

72
00:05:13,520 --> 00:05:15,000
They always stuck together.

73
00:05:17,160 --> 00:05:20,200
Her sister took care of her. Yeah.

74
00:05:24,720 --> 00:05:26,920
Sading told me she was distracted.

75
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:30,040
She was on her phone, playing games.

76
00:05:30,120 --> 00:05:33,560
She tried her best
to keep an eye on Chompoo.

77
00:05:36,960 --> 00:05:39,880
But the next moment, Chompoo disappeared.

78
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:48,480
When I looked into Sading's eyes,

79
00:05:48,560 --> 00:05:50,600
I could see her sadness.

80
00:05:51,640 --> 00:05:54,920
She'd always taken really good care
of her sister.

81
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:56,600
They were always together.

82
00:05:59,040 --> 00:06:03,320
Most of the time,
Chompoo would never go anywhere alone.

83
00:06:03,400 --> 00:06:05,280
She wouldn't go into the forest.

84
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:12,960
And then when evening came,

85
00:06:13,040 --> 00:06:16,680
I just had a feeling
that something wasn't right.

86
00:06:25,320 --> 00:06:26,720
Chompoo?

87
00:06:27,320 --> 00:06:29,000
Come back to Daddy.

88
00:06:31,120 --> 00:06:33,440
Very quickly, I began searching everywhere

89
00:06:33,520 --> 00:06:35,680
that I thought she could have gone.

90
00:06:36,280 --> 00:06:38,280
It's okay, Daddy's here.

91
00:06:39,720 --> 00:06:43,240
My partner and I searched
the forest together all night.

92
00:06:43,920 --> 00:06:44,920
Chompoo?

93
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:48,720
We called her name,
listening for any kind of response.

94
00:06:53,880 --> 00:06:57,080
That first night,
I didn't sleep at all until dawn.

95
00:06:59,600 --> 00:07:03,320
I was worried about where
my daughter could have gone,

96
00:07:03,880 --> 00:07:06,440
or whether someone had kidnapped her.

97
00:07:07,040 --> 00:07:11,040
CHOMPOO MISSING FOR 24 HOURS

98
00:07:11,120 --> 00:07:14,160
It's unbelievable that the farmers
in Mukdahan still haven't found her.

99
00:07:14,240 --> 00:07:17,640
Let us all support the search of Chompoo,
the three-year-old girl

100
00:07:17,720 --> 00:07:19,800
who has disappeared
without a trace from home.

101
00:07:19,880 --> 00:07:22,160
The village has come together
for the search,

102
00:07:22,240 --> 00:07:23,680
but there is still no sign of her.

103
00:07:23,760 --> 00:07:25,280
Nothing here. Let's go downstream.

104
00:07:25,360 --> 00:07:28,000
My niece disappeared
in the morning. I wasn't home.

105
00:07:28,600 --> 00:07:31,080
When Chompoo disappeared from the village,

106
00:07:32,680 --> 00:07:35,760
all the relatives gathered together
at her mother's house.

107
00:07:37,160 --> 00:07:39,200
She must have gone over there.

108
00:07:40,200 --> 00:07:44,680
Chompoo was the granddaughter
and the flesh and blood of Taen's family.

109
00:07:44,760 --> 00:07:46,880
We had the opportunity
to take care of her.

110
00:07:47,400 --> 00:07:50,120
Chompoo connected everyone.
If we fought, we'd stop for her.

111
00:07:50,200 --> 00:07:51,960
SOMPORN LARBPHO
"AUNT TAEN," CHOMPOO'S AUNT

112
00:07:52,040 --> 00:07:55,440
We loved each other so much
because of her.

113
00:08:00,280 --> 00:08:02,720
MANOP POLSAWANG
"UNCLE MOK," VILLAGER

114
00:08:02,800 --> 00:08:05,640
Sometimes, children get lost
in the forest.

115
00:08:08,160 --> 00:08:09,720
It's dangerous.

116
00:08:10,920 --> 00:08:12,920
There are snakes and mosquitoes.

117
00:08:14,080 --> 00:08:17,000
And what will they eat?
There's no food or water.

118
00:08:19,680 --> 00:08:23,040
Chompoo wouldn't just go with anyone,
and she wouldn't stray far.

119
00:08:27,120 --> 00:08:29,480
People were talking a lot about Chompoo.

120
00:08:29,560 --> 00:08:32,720
All they knew was she had disappeared
and that someone hurt her.

121
00:08:32,800 --> 00:08:35,080
But I didn't tell my sister
what people were saying.

122
00:08:35,160 --> 00:08:37,040
I didn't want her to get stressed.

123
00:08:37,120 --> 00:08:39,080
Chompoo is no longer with us.

124
00:08:39,720 --> 00:08:40,960
Oh, shit!

125
00:08:41,800 --> 00:08:42,760
Yes.

126
00:08:44,480 --> 00:08:47,440
More and more people showed up
to help search for her

127
00:08:47,520 --> 00:08:49,840
because she was nowhere to be found.

128
00:08:52,680 --> 00:08:56,160
<i>I went up and down</i>
<i>the mountain four or five times that day.</i>

129
00:08:58,600 --> 00:09:00,880
Officers from the Royal Forest Department

130
00:09:00,960 --> 00:09:02,360
were guided by the villagers…

131
00:09:02,440 --> 00:09:03,520
COMMUNITY FOREST AREA

132
00:09:03,600 --> 00:09:06,600
…as they were local
and knew the area well.

133
00:09:07,920 --> 00:09:12,160
CHOMPOO MISSING FOR 48 HOURS

134
00:09:13,880 --> 00:09:16,240
I made a post
about my child's disappearance

135
00:09:16,320 --> 00:09:17,480
and put my phone number on it.

136
00:09:17,560 --> 00:09:19,640
CHOMPOO IS MISSING
POST

137
00:09:20,520 --> 00:09:22,760
And then my phone kept ringing constantly.

138
00:09:22,840 --> 00:09:24,680
DISAPPEARED MAY 11 9:30 A.M.
KOK KORK VILLAGE

139
00:09:25,560 --> 00:09:26,760
Inside?

140
00:09:27,400 --> 00:09:29,600
Everyone was involved in the search.

141
00:09:31,720 --> 00:09:34,760
Check the ditch. Check it.
Check all the ditches.

142
00:09:41,320 --> 00:09:44,680
Everyone looked in the swamps
and everywhere around Kok Kork.

143
00:09:45,280 --> 00:09:49,520
Dear guardian spirit of the forest,
let them achieve the results desired.

144
00:09:49,600 --> 00:09:52,440
Is it on the right? Follow him.

145
00:09:53,600 --> 00:09:56,640
There were shamans and monks coming,

146
00:09:56,720 --> 00:09:58,720
saying Chompoo was here and there.

147
00:10:02,680 --> 00:10:05,040
Mediums told us to do this and that.
We did everything.

148
00:10:05,120 --> 00:10:07,120
PATCHARAMON PATCHARAPAT
"SAWITREE," CHOMPOO'S MOTHER

149
00:10:07,200 --> 00:10:09,160
May it be gold, be diamond, be glass.

150
00:10:09,240 --> 00:10:12,280
Does this mean
you mostly believed the shamans back then?

151
00:10:12,360 --> 00:10:14,520
Even if I didn't believe them,
I'd still do it.

152
00:10:17,400 --> 00:10:21,120
When the monks came to the village,
we followed their guidance,

153
00:10:21,200 --> 00:10:22,880
for peace of mind.

154
00:10:23,560 --> 00:10:24,440
We were hopeful.

155
00:10:24,920 --> 00:10:28,920
CHOMPOO MISSING FOR 72 HOURS

156
00:10:30,400 --> 00:10:33,040
By the fourth day of the search,
I was exhausted.

157
00:10:33,120 --> 00:10:35,120
-They're searching over there.
-That's it.

158
00:10:35,200 --> 00:10:36,640
-Yes, right there.
-Jud.

159
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:38,080
I couldn't walk anymore,

160
00:10:38,160 --> 00:10:41,280
because I had barely eaten
or drunk any water.

161
00:10:41,360 --> 00:10:45,440
I didn't sleep at all because I went out
to look for her whenever I could.

162
00:10:46,920 --> 00:10:48,400
I had a bad feeling.

163
00:10:49,440 --> 00:10:51,600
There wasn't even a place
for people to sit.

164
00:10:51,680 --> 00:10:53,960
And for me, I didn't even eat or drink.

165
00:10:54,040 --> 00:10:55,600
We've looked. Not here, nothing.

166
00:10:55,680 --> 00:11:00,280
Someone called and reported
that they saw a pair of shoes.

167
00:11:00,360 --> 00:11:01,280
Okay.

168
00:11:02,560 --> 00:11:05,360
They didn't specify
whether they were girls' or boys' shoes.

169
00:11:05,440 --> 00:11:06,280
Kids' shoes.

170
00:11:06,360 --> 00:11:08,360
But they said
they were little kids' shoes.

171
00:11:14,200 --> 00:11:16,600
Someone said
they had seen a pair of kids' shoes

172
00:11:16,680 --> 00:11:20,120
but didn't know whose they were,
so they came down to report them.

173
00:11:24,280 --> 00:11:25,800
Check up front, go up there.

174
00:11:25,880 --> 00:11:29,640
Yes.
If your soul is still here, come to us.

175
00:11:29,720 --> 00:11:32,440
-Where are you, my dear?
-Where are you?

176
00:11:32,520 --> 00:11:37,680
Many forest rangers, police officers,
and villagers went out that day.

177
00:11:37,760 --> 00:11:40,920
No less than 40 to 50 people
followed us up there.

178
00:11:42,520 --> 00:11:45,280
It seemed like spirits
were in the big trees.

179
00:11:45,360 --> 00:11:47,680
If we got close to them,
we got goosebumps.

180
00:11:47,760 --> 00:11:50,400
I'm getting goosebumps
just talking about them.

181
00:11:50,920 --> 00:11:54,280
It was dark,
so everyone walked up in a line.

182
00:11:54,360 --> 00:11:57,040
-Chompoo, where are you?
-Hey.

183
00:11:57,120 --> 00:11:59,200
-Hey.
-Where are you, Chompoo?

184
00:11:59,280 --> 00:12:01,840
We shone the flashlight
because it was dark.

185
00:12:03,520 --> 00:12:04,520
Hey.

186
00:12:05,200 --> 00:12:08,680
Hey, Chompoo, where are you?

187
00:12:11,080 --> 00:12:12,040
A snake.

188
00:12:12,120 --> 00:12:13,200
Hey!

189
00:12:13,280 --> 00:12:14,880
-Hey!
-Oh, dear.

190
00:12:14,960 --> 00:12:17,880
We saw the snake
and ran in different directions.

191
00:12:21,320 --> 00:12:23,320
And then I saw Chompoo's body.

192
00:12:28,640 --> 00:12:30,680
-We just found her!
-We found the child.

193
00:12:30,760 --> 00:12:33,520
We found the child.

194
00:12:33,600 --> 00:12:34,720
We found her.

195
00:12:34,800 --> 00:12:38,880
I decided to call my friend
who had joined the search.

196
00:12:40,520 --> 00:12:43,640
I asked him what was… what was happening.

197
00:12:43,720 --> 00:12:46,600
He paused and didn't say anything.

198
00:12:46,680 --> 00:12:48,880
And then he told me to stay calm.

199
00:12:49,400 --> 00:12:53,000
And I knew in my heart
that news wouldn't be good.

200
00:12:57,960 --> 00:12:59,800
I asked him over and over,

201
00:12:59,880 --> 00:13:02,720
"Just tell me. Tell me what's going on."

202
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:08,080
He told me that Chompoo…

203
00:13:09,440 --> 00:13:10,520
had gone…

204
00:13:12,120 --> 00:13:13,440
to a better place.

205
00:13:20,560 --> 00:13:23,560
-Calm down. Calm down.
-Oh, dear.

206
00:13:23,640 --> 00:13:24,760
Calm down.

207
00:13:30,080 --> 00:13:33,560
It's like someone taking
a knife and stabbing me repeatedly.

208
00:13:33,640 --> 00:13:36,080
I already knew
what condition my child was in.

209
00:13:36,600 --> 00:13:39,320
Don't tell me that my child was cold,
that she was in the forest,

210
00:13:39,400 --> 00:13:41,600
or that she was hungry or crying.

211
00:13:41,680 --> 00:13:42,520
I knew that.

212
00:13:44,520 --> 00:13:45,640
They just found it.

213
00:13:46,160 --> 00:13:47,800
{\an8}Why did it turn out this way?

214
00:13:47,880 --> 00:13:49,400
{\an8}At that time,

215
00:13:50,640 --> 00:13:52,680
there were so many f-- feelings.

216
00:13:54,560 --> 00:13:57,480
I was just very confused back then.

217
00:13:58,000 --> 00:13:59,560
{\an8}DIED: MAY 14, 2019 (4-YEAR-OLD)

218
00:13:59,640 --> 00:14:02,720
{\an8}It was more than just heartbreak.

219
00:14:06,200 --> 00:14:08,280
I lost my little girl,

220
00:14:08,360 --> 00:14:10,000
the apple of my eye.

221
00:14:11,920 --> 00:14:13,800
The person I loved the most.

222
00:14:17,120 --> 00:14:19,760
I didn't want to live
in this world without her.

223
00:14:24,080 --> 00:14:26,280
The picture of her lying on the ground…

224
00:14:27,840 --> 00:14:29,480
has stuck with me to this day.

225
00:14:33,680 --> 00:14:35,960
I prayed to Phra That Phanom,

226
00:14:36,040 --> 00:14:38,840
saying I would like
the culprit who killed her,

227
00:14:38,920 --> 00:14:42,760
whether intentionally or not,
to surrender.

228
00:14:42,840 --> 00:14:46,280
I would like them to confess or to repent.

229
00:14:51,160 --> 00:14:54,680
SAKHON NAKHON TEMPLE

230
00:14:54,760 --> 00:14:58,600
MARUAY MARKET
WONGSRICHA FAMILY

231
00:15:03,280 --> 00:15:06,480
The images that are still with me

232
00:15:06,560 --> 00:15:08,760
are those of Chompoo
running around playing

233
00:15:08,840 --> 00:15:12,080
with her aunt,
her parents and grandparents.

234
00:15:12,680 --> 00:15:14,600
Those images are all in my memory.

235
00:15:16,600 --> 00:15:18,640
Ladies and gentlemen, regarding the case

236
00:15:18,720 --> 00:15:21,400
of Chompoo, the three-year-old-girl,
which we have been following…

237
00:15:21,480 --> 00:15:22,640
Yes.

238
00:15:22,720 --> 00:15:24,680
…she was found yesterday.

239
00:15:24,760 --> 00:15:26,920
However, she was already deceased.

240
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:32,000
The authorities immediately deployed
forces up there.

241
00:15:32,080 --> 00:15:36,240
They went to the Phu Lek Fai Forest
in the Phu Pha Yon National Park.

242
00:15:36,320 --> 00:15:38,280
The terrain here is quite difficult.

243
00:15:38,360 --> 00:15:40,400
Aside from very steep slopes,

244
00:15:40,480 --> 00:15:43,000
the paths here were
quite difficult to walk

245
00:15:43,080 --> 00:15:46,520
because it was full
of small and big rocks all over the place.

246
00:15:46,600 --> 00:15:48,000
{\an8}DISAPPEARED HERE - FOUND HERE
KM

247
00:15:48,080 --> 00:15:52,720
{\an8}There's no way that she could have walked
up to the area where the body was found.

248
00:15:53,600 --> 00:15:56,400
One thing we could immediately tell
upon finding the body…

249
00:15:56,480 --> 00:15:57,800
SARAWAT KIJPANIT
"ICE" - REPORTER

250
00:15:57,880 --> 00:16:00,080
…was she couldn't
have walked there on her own.

251
00:16:00,160 --> 00:16:03,680
If she couldn't have got there on her own,
someone must have taken her there.

252
00:16:03,760 --> 00:16:06,600
As a result, the case is being considered
as a possible murder.

253
00:16:08,040 --> 00:16:10,000
1,390 COMMENTS
I HOPE THEY GET…

254
00:16:10,080 --> 00:16:11,120
POST COMMENT

255
00:16:11,200 --> 00:16:12,480
SOMEONE MUST HAVE DONE IT

256
00:16:12,560 --> 00:16:15,320
I HOPE THEY GET THE PERPETRATOR.
PEOPLE THESE DAYS ARE SCARY

257
00:16:15,400 --> 00:16:18,960
PLEASE BRING THE CRIMINAL TO JUSTICE

258
00:16:21,560 --> 00:16:25,720
Since there were no forensic tools
like CCTV cameras there,

259
00:16:25,800 --> 00:16:27,560
and it happened in a forest,

260
00:16:27,640 --> 00:16:30,120
all we could do was
to interrogate witnesses,

261
00:16:30,200 --> 00:16:31,680
as detectives always do.

262
00:16:32,360 --> 00:16:34,640
We also tried to get close
to people around the victim,

263
00:16:34,720 --> 00:16:36,840
stationed officers at the scene,

264
00:16:36,920 --> 00:16:38,240
and monitored their behavior,

265
00:16:38,320 --> 00:16:40,600
including emotions and feelings,

266
00:16:40,680 --> 00:16:43,600
body language,
facial expressions, and actions.

267
00:16:43,680 --> 00:16:45,760
We looked at everything together.

268
00:16:45,840 --> 00:16:49,400
We had to go
back to basic investigation principles.

269
00:16:49,480 --> 00:16:50,440
Thank you.

270
00:16:50,520 --> 00:16:51,840
Are you Kaewta?

271
00:16:51,920 --> 00:16:55,120
-The weather's hot.
-I don't have problems these days.

272
00:16:55,920 --> 00:16:58,920
When the investigation started, we…

273
00:16:59,440 --> 00:17:01,520
we were being questioned constantly.

274
00:17:08,160 --> 00:17:11,800
Whatever the police asked us,
we answered truthfully.

275
00:17:11,880 --> 00:17:13,720
We told them everything,

276
00:17:13,800 --> 00:17:18,160
because we wanted to know
everything that had happened to our child.

277
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:24,600
{\an8}KITTISAK WEERACHAICHAROENSUK
JOURNALIST

278
00:17:24,680 --> 00:17:28,120
{\an8}Back then, I was already covering crime
in the Northeast,

279
00:17:28,200 --> 00:17:31,000
so the station sent me to Mukdahan.

280
00:17:31,080 --> 00:17:33,680
Now we walked in to the temple archway.

281
00:17:33,760 --> 00:17:35,320
This is the entrance.

282
00:17:39,080 --> 00:17:42,600
At first, I thought it would
be very challenging, and it was.

283
00:17:46,160 --> 00:17:48,480
The villagers were very rural people.

284
00:17:48,560 --> 00:17:52,320
I went looking for the CCTV cameras.
There were none.

285
00:17:52,400 --> 00:17:54,400
I didn't know what to do.

286
00:17:55,480 --> 00:17:58,400
-Someone came.
-Tell them they were gone.

287
00:17:58,480 --> 00:18:01,480
<i>Officials said that everything found</i>

288
00:18:01,560 --> 00:18:05,720
<i>near the child's body, along the path,</i>
<i>before discovering her body,</i>

289
00:18:05,800 --> 00:18:07,720
<i>is considered evidence.</i>

290
00:18:08,480 --> 00:18:10,040
They went somewhere else.

291
00:18:10,120 --> 00:18:12,080
<i>The only evidence that hasn't been found</i>

292
00:18:12,160 --> 00:18:16,000
<i>is a shirt she wore when she disappeared.</i>
<i>She was naked when they found her body.</i>

293
00:18:16,080 --> 00:18:18,960
<i>Someone took her shirt.</i>
<i>What did they need it for?</i>

294
00:18:21,160 --> 00:18:22,880
I couldn't believe my eyes.

295
00:18:22,960 --> 00:18:25,720
She was lying there still like a doll.

296
00:18:28,320 --> 00:18:30,720
She was lying on her back,

297
00:18:32,240 --> 00:18:33,760
facing this way.

298
00:18:34,880 --> 00:18:37,160
Her legs were spread apart.

299
00:18:40,240 --> 00:18:41,840
She was completely naked.

300
00:18:44,600 --> 00:18:48,000
Almost all the men
in the village became suspects.

301
00:18:48,760 --> 00:18:50,480
Why was it only men?

302
00:18:50,560 --> 00:18:54,120
Because when they found
the body of Chompoo,

303
00:18:54,200 --> 00:18:59,160
she… she was not wearing
anything below the waist.

304
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:04,760
The police did DNA testing
on almost all the men in the village.

305
00:19:08,960 --> 00:19:12,200
We suspected it was a drug addict,

306
00:19:12,280 --> 00:19:13,880
a sex offender,

307
00:19:13,960 --> 00:19:17,120
or someone who had a conflict
with her parents.

308
00:19:17,200 --> 00:19:19,640
That's what we initially suspected.

309
00:19:24,160 --> 00:19:28,720
For this investigation, we need
to be more meticulous and detailed.

310
00:19:28,800 --> 00:19:31,320
And we'll also be expanding
the inspection area.

311
00:19:31,400 --> 00:19:33,080
It'll take some time.

312
00:19:33,600 --> 00:19:34,760
I can't say much now.

313
00:19:40,160 --> 00:19:41,320
Watch out, the branches.

314
00:19:41,400 --> 00:19:44,040
The villagers kept the body
and sent it for an autopsy.

315
00:19:45,800 --> 00:19:48,720
-Yes, there is. Look carefully.
-We've put her in the car.

316
00:19:51,080 --> 00:19:53,960
Chompoo's death has left her family
with unanswered questions.

317
00:19:54,040 --> 00:19:56,400
They've accepted those answers
may not come.

318
00:19:56,480 --> 00:19:58,400
<i>However, the initial autopsy result</i>

319
00:19:58,480 --> 00:20:01,760
<i>from the Sunpasitthiprasong Hospital</i>
<i>in Ubon Ratchathani</i>

320
00:20:01,840 --> 00:20:05,640
<i>found no evidence</i>
<i>of sexual assault or physical abuse.</i>

321
00:20:05,720 --> 00:20:07,800
<i>But the family still has doubts.</i>

322
00:20:10,080 --> 00:20:11,560
You'll notice

323
00:20:11,640 --> 00:20:15,240
that the body underwent
examination three times.

324
00:20:15,960 --> 00:20:19,280
Now, the first examination
by the Dong Luang Hospital

325
00:20:19,360 --> 00:20:21,280
didn't include an autopsy.

326
00:20:21,360 --> 00:20:22,560
The second report was done

327
00:20:22,640 --> 00:20:26,960
by the Sunpasitthiprasong Hospital
in Ubon Ratchathani.

328
00:20:28,240 --> 00:20:30,680
Now, based on the results of the autopsy,

329
00:20:30,760 --> 00:20:32,880
they couldn't indicate the cause of death.

330
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:37,320
But the child's parents have
expressed their concerns,

331
00:20:37,400 --> 00:20:41,840
as they still have doubts
about the cause of death.

332
00:20:41,920 --> 00:20:46,560
The re-examinations were conducted
for this reason.

333
00:20:46,640 --> 00:20:51,080
The third report was produced
by the Institute of Forensic Medicine,

334
00:20:51,160 --> 00:20:52,960
Police General Hospital.

335
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:58,440
Officers came to take the body
for another examination in Bangkok.

336
00:21:00,080 --> 00:21:01,720
It was for an autopsy.

337
00:21:01,800 --> 00:21:04,440
-The Police General Hospital.
-Another round of autopsy in Bangkok.

338
00:21:05,480 --> 00:21:08,080
The police asked
if any relatives were going.

339
00:21:09,120 --> 00:21:11,400
And since no one was,
Uncle Phol volunteered.

340
00:21:11,480 --> 00:21:13,720
INSTITUTE OF FORENSIC MEDICINE

341
00:21:15,440 --> 00:21:17,880
<i>The uncle says he hopes the perpetrator</i>

342
00:21:17,960 --> 00:21:19,480
<i>isn't someone in the village.</i>

343
00:21:19,560 --> 00:21:23,320
<i>If it turns out to be a local,</i>
<i>he'll have to worry for a long time,</i>

344
00:21:23,400 --> 00:21:26,280
<i>because the perpetrator</i>
<i>still hasn't been found.</i>

345
00:21:26,360 --> 00:21:29,760
The journalists must have
seen me talking about the case,

346
00:21:29,840 --> 00:21:33,080
so they were interested
in interviewing me for my opinions.

347
00:21:35,440 --> 00:21:37,840
And why not? I wasn't afraid
of speaking to the media.

348
00:21:37,920 --> 00:21:41,280
If it's a kidnapping,
the culprit is absolutely heartless.

349
00:21:43,760 --> 00:21:47,480
Also, we can't clearly say
whether the death was caused

350
00:21:47,560 --> 00:21:51,400
by starvation, dehydration, or murder.

351
00:21:51,480 --> 00:21:52,960
We can't clearly tell that.

352
00:21:54,720 --> 00:21:58,280
Therefore, regarding Chompoo's death,

353
00:21:58,360 --> 00:22:01,640
we still cannot identify
what exactly caused it.

354
00:22:03,760 --> 00:22:05,880
So people started to get curious again.

355
00:22:07,760 --> 00:22:10,640
We became more and more interested in it,
and the audience began

356
00:22:10,720 --> 00:22:12,320
to follow it more closely.

357
00:22:14,120 --> 00:22:16,880
She would never go with a stranger.

358
00:22:16,960 --> 00:22:19,040
She would only go with someone she knew.

359
00:22:21,680 --> 00:22:23,400
If we believe this,

360
00:22:25,160 --> 00:22:28,000
we must find someone
who could approach Chompoo

361
00:22:28,080 --> 00:22:29,840
without making her cry.

362
00:22:29,920 --> 00:22:31,920
The following is what we're considering.

363
00:22:32,000 --> 00:22:36,240
The person was known to her,
close to her, and could take her places.

364
00:22:37,600 --> 00:22:40,080
When viewers followed the case closely…

365
00:22:42,040 --> 00:22:44,200
it became strange

366
00:22:44,280 --> 00:22:48,360
that so many people were interested
in the death of a child.

367
00:22:48,440 --> 00:22:49,920
That made it strange.

368
00:22:50,000 --> 00:22:53,240
A child went missing
and was found dead on a mountain.

369
00:22:53,960 --> 00:22:56,400
But why were people so interested in it?

370
00:22:56,480 --> 00:22:58,520
A huge number of people were.

371
00:22:59,480 --> 00:23:01,600
Each channel had its own angle and story.

372
00:23:02,280 --> 00:23:05,240
But yesterday,
Thairath TV's field reporters

373
00:23:05,320 --> 00:23:07,520
received information from a villager.

374
00:23:09,840 --> 00:23:13,840
He said that Chompoo's parents
could be the perpetrators.

375
00:23:13,920 --> 00:23:18,600
If they were so worried about their child,
why didn't they actively search for her?

376
00:23:19,440 --> 00:23:21,840
Police officers often came to visit me,

377
00:23:21,920 --> 00:23:24,040
and ask if I suspected my sister.

378
00:23:24,120 --> 00:23:26,400
They would ask,
"Why didn't she go up the mountain?"

379
00:23:26,480 --> 00:23:28,040
They questioned everything.

380
00:23:29,640 --> 00:23:31,720
Back then, they blamed us,

381
00:23:31,800 --> 00:23:35,520
asking why we didn't take good care of her
and why we lost her.

382
00:23:36,200 --> 00:23:38,640
It was because of us, it was our fault.

383
00:23:38,720 --> 00:23:40,160
Uncle Phol said that.

384
00:23:46,600 --> 00:23:49,000
I wanted to ask this of her parents.

385
00:23:50,320 --> 00:23:54,080
Why haven't they gone
up Phu Lek Fai mountain until this day?

386
00:23:54,800 --> 00:23:55,960
They weren't even there

387
00:23:56,040 --> 00:23:58,600
when the monks guided
Chompoo's spirit back down.

388
00:23:59,720 --> 00:24:01,000
CHOMPOO'S MOM… WHY DID YOU…

389
00:24:01,520 --> 00:24:02,720
CHOMPOO DISAPPEARED…

390
00:24:02,800 --> 00:24:04,040
{\an8}PHOL MUST BE VERY SAD

391
00:24:04,120 --> 00:24:06,040
{\an8}UNLIKE HER PARENTS, WHO AREN'T SAD AT ALL

392
00:24:06,120 --> 00:24:09,280
{\an8}MA'AM, WHY DIDN'T YOU GO UP THE MOUNTAIN
TO LOOK FOR YOUR CHILD'S BODY?

393
00:24:09,360 --> 00:24:12,760
{\an8}SOMEONE WHO TRULY LOVES THEIR CHILD
SHOULDN'T CLAIM TO BE TOO TIRED

394
00:24:12,840 --> 00:24:15,200
{\an8}ISN'T IT STRANGE?
THE PARENTS WAITED AT HOME FOR NEWS

395
00:24:15,280 --> 00:24:17,640
{\an8}WHILE THE VILLAGERS WENT LOOKING
FOR THE KID AT NIGHT

396
00:24:17,720 --> 00:24:20,400
Do you insist
that you'd never hurt your child?

397
00:24:20,480 --> 00:24:21,320
Yes.

398
00:24:22,280 --> 00:24:25,200
If the person saying this has evidence,
then come arrest me.

399
00:24:25,280 --> 00:24:29,000
To the person who said this,
please don't make baseless accusations.

400
00:24:32,520 --> 00:24:34,880
We were angry, very angry,

401
00:24:35,520 --> 00:24:37,680
but we didn't respond to any of it.

402
00:24:43,160 --> 00:24:47,000
We had to be patient
and let the legal process run its course.

403
00:24:50,280 --> 00:24:53,840
At that time, we didn't give interviews
or talk to the media.

404
00:24:56,080 --> 00:24:59,400
We didn't explain anything
or speak publicly about it.

405
00:24:59,480 --> 00:25:00,960
We just stayed quiet

406
00:25:01,040 --> 00:25:03,840
and cooperated
with the police investigation.

407
00:25:05,120 --> 00:25:10,000
Sometimes, I interviewed Chompoo's parents
until they became mad at me.

408
00:25:10,080 --> 00:25:11,840
Her mother isn't good with words.

409
00:25:11,920 --> 00:25:15,040
She didn't appear much
in the media or cry,

410
00:25:15,120 --> 00:25:18,280
so the villagers were like,
"She killed her own child."

411
00:25:18,360 --> 00:25:21,560
I THOUGHT HER MOM NEVER HIKED
THE MOUNTAIN, BUT NOW SHE SAYS SHE DID!

412
00:25:21,640 --> 00:25:24,200
{\an8}BEFORE, A FOREST FORAGER SAID
HE HEARD TWO MEN'S VOICES

413
00:25:24,280 --> 00:25:26,640
{\an8}WERE THEY HER DAD AND OTHER UNCLE?!
THEY SEEM CLOSE

414
00:25:26,720 --> 00:25:29,640
{\an8}I SUSPECT HER PARENTS THE MOST.
HER BODY WAS CAREFULLY PLACED…

415
00:25:29,720 --> 00:25:32,240
I'M SICK OF SAWITREE ALWAYS ACCUSING PHOL

416
00:25:32,320 --> 00:25:35,000
THE WHOLE COUNTRY SUSPECTS HER
AND HER HUSBAND

417
00:25:35,080 --> 00:25:36,680
SHE SHOULD QUESTION HERSELF

418
00:25:39,880 --> 00:25:43,640
People were watching the news
and came to ask us about it.

419
00:25:43,720 --> 00:25:46,440
They came to us, and so we told them.

420
00:25:46,520 --> 00:25:48,160
And then they betrayed us.

421
00:25:48,240 --> 00:25:51,320
They did it by talking in the media
and social media channels.

422
00:25:51,400 --> 00:25:52,240
1,190 COMMENTS

423
00:25:52,320 --> 00:25:53,960
KARMA IS…
COMMENT

424
00:25:54,040 --> 00:25:55,960
{\an8}HOW AWFUL.
THIS WOMAN KEEPS CAUSING TROUBLE

425
00:25:56,040 --> 00:25:58,000
{\an8}KARMA IS CATCHING UP TO THE SINNER

426
00:25:58,080 --> 00:26:02,320
{\an8}Their betrayal hurt,
and it led to a false impression of us.

427
00:26:02,400 --> 00:26:05,000
{\an8}So we went online to defend ourselves.

428
00:26:05,640 --> 00:26:08,600
We just got attacked in the comments.

429
00:26:08,680 --> 00:26:10,000
It was horrible.

430
00:26:11,720 --> 00:26:14,040
MA'AM, DIDN'T YOU THINK
YOUR CHILD COULD BE FEELING HOT?

431
00:26:14,120 --> 00:26:16,680
IS OBSCENITY ALL THAT YOU COULD THINK OF?

432
00:26:17,520 --> 00:26:20,280
{\an8}LECTURER DR. TRYNH PHORAKSA
CRIMINOLOGIST

433
00:26:20,360 --> 00:26:22,720
Our society is full of bias,

434
00:26:22,800 --> 00:26:26,120
and has emotional expectations of others.

435
00:26:26,200 --> 00:26:30,600
They expect others to act
according to their expectations.

436
00:26:31,400 --> 00:26:33,280
Take sadness, for example.

437
00:26:33,360 --> 00:26:36,800
When the child disappeared,
you say, "Why aren't they sad?"

438
00:26:36,880 --> 00:26:38,560
The parents might be sad,

439
00:26:38,640 --> 00:26:42,320
but their emotional expression
doesn't meet your expectations.

440
00:26:42,400 --> 00:26:45,240
It doesn't reach the level <i>you </i>have set.

441
00:26:46,880 --> 00:26:49,360
We told ourselves, "Just survive."

442
00:26:50,520 --> 00:26:52,560
"We'll find out the result tomorrow."

443
00:26:53,280 --> 00:26:55,400
"We just have to get through all this."

444
00:27:03,200 --> 00:27:05,640
SONGPON RUENGSAMUT
PHOTOJOURNALIST

445
00:27:05,720 --> 00:27:08,920
The media gave importance to the family,

446
00:27:09,000 --> 00:27:11,000
as well as Uncle Phol.

447
00:27:16,840 --> 00:27:18,920
Her parents were selective
talking to the media.

448
00:27:19,000 --> 00:27:23,040
It was like… the media
was on a different side.

449
00:27:23,120 --> 00:27:24,400
Okay.

450
00:27:26,680 --> 00:27:28,960
One channel was
at Chompoo's mother's house,

451
00:27:29,040 --> 00:27:30,960
while the other was based
at Thorn's house,

452
00:27:31,040 --> 00:27:34,080
mainly interviewing me, Taen, and Thorn.

453
00:27:34,160 --> 00:27:38,160
Check, check, check, check, check.
One, two, three. One, two, three.

454
00:27:38,240 --> 00:27:40,240
Between the two channels,

455
00:27:40,800 --> 00:27:45,200
the coverage from Thorn's house
gained an enormous following.

456
00:27:45,280 --> 00:27:46,720
The viewership kept climbing.

457
00:27:46,800 --> 00:27:47,880
Yes.

458
00:27:47,960 --> 00:27:50,360
The kids like you a lot.
Do you wanna see him?

459
00:27:50,440 --> 00:27:51,320
Let me see.

460
00:27:51,400 --> 00:27:53,120
It shot to the top of the ranks,

461
00:27:53,200 --> 00:27:56,400
{\an8}surpassing Thailand's
most popular TV drama,

462
00:27:56,480 --> 00:27:58,280
{\an8}and reaching the number one spot.

463
00:27:58,360 --> 00:28:00,040
{\an8}The coverage of the channel was up there.

464
00:28:08,520 --> 00:28:11,640
It's difficult for news
to beat dramas in ratings.

465
00:28:11,720 --> 00:28:12,600
The abbot will…

466
00:28:12,680 --> 00:28:15,800
The news ratings jumped
up to the top three.

467
00:28:16,800 --> 00:28:18,400
It was extraordinary.

468
00:28:18,480 --> 00:28:20,200
{\an8}-Well…
-All right, Uncle Phol.

469
00:28:20,280 --> 00:28:21,800
-Uncle Phol. Start filming.
-Yes?

470
00:28:21,880 --> 00:28:25,800
After you arrived, what have you found?
And why did you come here?

471
00:28:25,880 --> 00:28:28,360
My boss had sent me to cover Uncle Phol.

472
00:28:28,440 --> 00:28:30,480
Okay, let's get in the car.

473
00:28:31,680 --> 00:28:34,920
I've stopped the timer. I've stopped it.

474
00:28:35,000 --> 00:28:37,480
He turned on the music and sang along.

475
00:28:37,560 --> 00:28:40,720
I sat in the back and filmed
him singing while driving.

476
00:28:46,200 --> 00:28:47,480
I sent it to my boss.

477
00:28:47,560 --> 00:28:51,720
The viewers commented
on how beautiful his voice was.

478
00:28:51,800 --> 00:28:57,560
<i>The days, months, years</i>
<i>That I've been through in life </i>

479
00:28:57,640 --> 00:29:00,400
<i>With twists and turns </i>

480
00:29:00,480 --> 00:29:04,680
<i>I can't escape it, or get lost </i>

481
00:29:04,760 --> 00:29:07,360
<i>It's the same old path repeatedly </i>

482
00:29:07,440 --> 00:29:09,640
<i>There's no way to escape… </i>

483
00:29:13,040 --> 00:29:14,440
Thank you.

484
00:29:14,520 --> 00:29:16,800
The journalists were very excited

485
00:29:16,880 --> 00:29:20,520
because their coverage had ratings
surpassing those of the dramas.

486
00:29:20,600 --> 00:29:22,840
-Take it with you, Uncle Phol.
